/how-to-use-spin-wheel-classroom-examples#faq\",\n      \"mainEntity\": [\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"How many student names can I add?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"You can add up to 500 entries per wheel—plenty for any homeroom roster or grade-level assembly. For larger groups where tiny slices are hard to read on a projector, consider spinning seating rows or group numbers first.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Is the selection genuinely random?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Yes — the tool draws unbiased values using the browser's Web Cryptography API (window.crypto.getRandomValues) with rejection sampling, giving every entry an exact mathematical chance before the visual animation starts.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Can I use it on an interactive whiteboard?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Yes — it is browser-based and works on Chromebooks, iPads, and interactive whiteboards. Fullscreen mode provides crisp visibility across the room and works smoothly with touch displays.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"What if the same student keeps getting picked?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Switch ON Remove Winner After Spin in Settings so each chosen student leaves the wheel until everyone has participated before reloading the roster.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Can I give some students better odds, as a reward?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"