        <h2 id="conclusion">9. Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
          A spin wheel is one of the few classroom tools that costs nothing,
          takes minutes to set up, and genuinely improves both atmosphere and
          fairness from the first use. It solves a problem every teacher hits
          constantly: how to select students, assign tasks, and run activities
          in a way that feels neutral and visibly fair.
        </p>
        <p>
          The activities here are starting points — the most effective classroom
          wheels get shaped around your own students and subject. Start with
          cold-calling on a name wheel, since it's the easiest entry point, and
          build from there.
        </p>
        <p>
          The students who surprise you most are usually the ones who never
          volunteer. The wheel gives them the same shot as everyone else, and
          they often have the best answers.
